Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["A Working Tour of the Symmetry Functions", "Title",
 CellID->509267359,ExpressionUUID->"4ddb5767-1f00-4973-a411-49eacd07850d"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This tutorial walks through every function in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Wolfram`TensorNetworks`Symmetry`", "InlineCode"]], "InlineCode",
  ExpressionUUID->"836b25da-f2a0-4a38-a020-def30a2f77f9"],
 " in the order a tensor-network practitioner meets them. After it you can \
(i) decide whether a partition or a tableau is the right object for a \
problem, (ii) predict the size of every block of a symmetry-resolved tensor \
in closed form, and (iii) project a TN tensor onto the \
irreducible-representation subspace it physically belongs to. Every claim is \
paired with a Wolfram Language cell; nothing is asserted without being \
computed."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"0db7ce3d-cb0d-4fb9-a187-6c80bde1ee8d"],

Cell["\<\
The arc starts at two indistinguishable particles and walks up the rank, \
picking up one Symmetry function per step. By the end all sixteen exported \
functions appear at least once on a tensor with a tensor-network reason to \
exist.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"dd49c465-9c78-4836-bb51-9f97fb9bed4f"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Inventory", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"a144f926-f9ee-4345-b414-a90c41a2f459"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Symmetry layer exports sixteen symbols. Six handle the ",
 StyleBox["combinatorics", "TI"],
 " of Young diagrams. Two are typed ",
 StyleBox["accessors", "TI"],
 " for the row and column structure of a tableau. Six are ",
 StyleBox["dimensions", "TI"],
 " of the irreducible-representation blocks, split between the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["S", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "193f8c1c-c0c2-4d75-89d9-4f3b930d30cb"],
 " side (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"dim", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["V", "TI"], "\[Lambda]"]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"4199d2c4-b5a4-4a59-87dc-184b76947dcf"],
 ") and the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["G", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["L", "TI"], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"741bbc07-427e-46d7-aa4b-4034ca7721b6"],
 " side (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"dim", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["W", "TI"], "\[Lambda]"], 
    RowBox[{"(", 
     StyleBox["d", "TI"], ")"}]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"3eadb88e-2cb0-4441-a9c2-c4206c09b03f"],
 "). Two are ",
 StyleBox["tensor actions", "TI"],
 " that produce a tensor in a chosen symmetry class."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"d74a6dc9-e78e-4a7c-891f-cb00fefefafe"],

