 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"0636a641-3ee7-42d4-a4d0-8853e1e0142c"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "This is everything you need to declare \"this tensor is symmetric in slots \
1, 2\", \"this matrix is Hermitian\", \"this rank-4 tensor antisymmetrises in \
",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", "2"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"0001f7e6-2f16-4810-b81f-92ccf009dd05"],
 " and in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"(", 
    RowBox[{"3", ",", "4"}], ")"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"a2136f67-6fad-4b6a-82f9-4524ae9f3c7d"],
 " and is invariant under swapping the pairs\". It is not enough to declare \
\"",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"a", "b", "c", "d"}], "TI"]], "+", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"a", "c", "d", "b"}], "TI"]], "+", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"a", "d", "b", "c"}], "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", "0"}], 
   TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "33e9cba4-57d9-4173-bd05-fb17be28c1ed"],
 "\": that is a ",
 StyleBox["multi-term", "TI"],
 " relation (three permuted copies summing to zero) and lies outside the \
mono-term language. The same gap is what blocks Young projection onto a \
mixed-symmetry irreducible representation: those projectors are \
sums-with-signs over the group on each row and each column of a Young \
diagram, and the image is defined by satisfying ",
 StyleBox["several", "TI"],
 " permutation relations together, not one."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1557b750-650b-4adb-8987-85a66ccd87e8"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Symmetry functions in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  StyleBox["Wolfram`TensorNetworks`Symmetry`", "InlineCode"]], "InlineCode",
  ExpressionUUID->"8921d8af-2f7b-44c9-94aa-f485e74e3bc5"],
 " fill exactly this gap. Its ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "YoungProject"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "09d74bba-ca12-4467-a519-ac1b80c13187"],
 " produces tensors that lie in ",
 StyleBox["one ", "TI"],
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["S", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "63144f62-75bf-4cf7-b40c-6c063caeb739"],
 StyleBox[" irreducible representation", "TI"],
 ", a condition that always implies extra multi-term identities. The Riemann \
curvature tensor is the canonical example: living in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"2", ",", "2"}], "}"}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"a16dfd17-0d85-4d66-aa93-f791f66f9a1c"],
 " irreducible representation simultaneously satisfies pair-antisymmetry ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"a", "b", "c", "d"}], "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", "-", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"b", "a", "c", "d"}], "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"3bc2d452-d783-47e3-889a-e215189672bb"],
 ", pair-antisymmetry ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"a", "b", "c", "d"}], "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", "-", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"a", "b", "d", "c"}], "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"2b34e093-82e4-4e32-90fc-71f84a978cf4"],
 ", pair-swap ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"a", "b", "c", "d"}], "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"c", "d", "a", "b"}], "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"15f0d429-0d56-4200-ac02-07a2b5214f7d"],
 ", ",
 StyleBox["and", "TI"],
 " the algebraic first Bianchi identity ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"a", "b", "c", "d"}], "TI"]], "+", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"a", "c", "d", "b"}], "TI"]], "+", 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["R", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"a", "d", "b", "c"}], "TI"]], "\[LongEqual]", "0"}], 
   TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "ade1911c-3499-46a3-a4bb-2d6868c28468"],
 ". The three pair conditions are mono-term and reachable by built-in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "Symmetrize"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "5a0d0ea6-c66c-40e9-9543-ffbbf3e87ffc"],
 "; the Bianchi identity is multi-term and is not."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"8dc33566-bfdd-4228-b65e-9308ea909106"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The Riemann-tensor example later in the tutorial makes this concrete: \
built-in ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "Symmetrize"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "ed384fd1-3f48-41ab-88a3-c516017413bf"],
 " with the three Riemann pair generators leaves a finite Bianchi residual, \
while ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "YoungProject"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "331c89f9-ee65-495c-ab4e-bd4c7a5416b1"],
 " zeroes it. The map between the two layers:"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"4dd29766-e694-40d9-b79d-7ca1dab8f4cb"],

Cell[BoxData[GridBox[{
   {Cell["Operation", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"7cd93f59-a2e6-435f-abb0-cb2da10e704b"],
     Cell["Built-in WL", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"23146cf2-8057-44c3-aa59-4fc3846353e5"],
     Cell["Symmetry functions", "TableText",
     FontWeight->Bold,ExpressionUUID->"3c23e440-da80-4207-8d0e-0d067ad78ca4"]},
   {Cell["Mono-term symmetrise (boson, fermion, Riemann pair)", "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"67edf9c0-6ef1-4936-b685-cd915a2ed909"], Cell[TextData[
    Cell[BoxData[
     RowBox[{"Symmetrize", "[", 
      RowBox[{"T", ",", " ", "sym"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
     "ee085af7-547a-44f1-bc89-1143ea0dee5e"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "bec4c7d3-50e1-48e7-a8c3-f94907cd2d94"], Cell[
    "(wrapped by the Symmetry functions)", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "75c705d0-7163-409d-bc5f-ba0791ce4c59"]},
   {Cell["Detect mono-term symmetry group", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "383435f0-890a-4a6a-9ff3-b963442e22f9"], Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
     RowBox[{"TensorSymmetry", "[", "T", "]"}]], "InlineFormula",
     ExpressionUUID->"81cafda3-07aa-48a0-9952-0b1284fc9b61"]], "TableText",
     ExpressionUUID->"e855df09-7562-48af-b0d8-4edc3b4dc66c"], Cell[
    "(no analogue)", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "2e9eed21-b39b-4c2d-81b1-d0a37fceb2ed"]},
   {Cell["Compressed storage by orbit", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "95ff7c6a-a4e3-4df7-b437-9a33c3a4891f"], Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
    "SymmetrizedArray"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
     "01ccb9f2-eec2-418f-bb46-dd141ccd980a"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "4858cf9b-95bf-4fdb-8250-641152db1e19"], Cell[TextData[{
     "(no analogue; the Symmetry functions emit dense / ",
     Cell[BoxData[
     "Normal"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
      "c87f3917-4fe6-4874-a819-95a1725a8263"],
     ")"
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"1bb7dda8-489d-451f-8d18-251c09355ff3"]},
   {Cell["Single-tableau / mixed-symmetry projection (multi-term)", 
     "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"1975822c-027a-496d-864e-786772ece940"], 
    Cell["(not supported)", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "ca095c1c-b491-4e5b-8fd1-0916bcca4fc6"], Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
     RowBox[{"YoungProject", "[", 
      RowBox[{"T", ",", " ", "tab"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
     "e7d85553-b6d8-4ad9-ad72-4930f2781dfa"]], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "ec0d6a27-4402-4eee-8db0-5a90ffbcb350"]},
   {Cell[TextData[{
     "Irreducible representation dimension ",
     Cell[BoxData[
      FormBox[
       RowBox[{"dim", 
        SubscriptBox[
         StyleBox["V", "TI"], "\[Lambda]"]}], TraditionalForm]], 
      "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"91382965-e0f8-4c71-b448-5bd70fc3d5b7"],
     
     " via hook formula"
    }], "TableText",ExpressionUUID->"23b7855e-4564-457c-817a-de05273bfc14"], 
    Cell["(not supported)", "TableText",ExpressionUUID->
     "5489409d-46b4-4117-9117-772c6d94336d"], Cell[TextData[Cell[BoxData[
