 CellID->911080844,ExpressionUUID->"fc606307-0c59-4668-ae06-247430787031"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Hermiticity is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
 "ConjugateTranspose"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "dbf984c5-a695-4a38-965c-cf045db34a9b"],
 " (transpose composed with conjugation) and lives in built-in WL's ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  RowBox[{"Hermitian", "[", 
   RowBox[{"{", 
    RowBox[{"1", ",", "2"}], "}"}], "]"}]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "ff74cdde-9cba-4829-aa8e-fda42a77457e"],
 " symmetry head, not in the ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox[
    StyleBox["S", "TI"], 
    StyleBox["n", "TI"]], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "76a9e538-fba0-4219-88ee-53a1f8dc999e"],
 " representation theory the Symmetry functions implement. The two layers \
compose without collapsing: a tensor can be Hermitian without being \
symmetric, and the Young projector touches only the symmetric / antisymmetric \
layer."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"26343d33-c82f-4612-afad-b3ce64eaef5f"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Block-sparse Frobenius contraction on a rank-3 bond", "Subsubsection",ExpressionUUID->"dea90935-c927-4348-9afe-4e954e2b41e9"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Contracting two rank-3 tensors splits cleanly along symmetry \
sectors: only same-sector pieces talk. ", "TI"],
 Cell[BoxData[
 "YoungProject"], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "a19dae4b-887c-48f3-8fc4-85ff4fad92c7"],
 StyleBox[" decomposes each tensor into its bosonic, parastatistical, and \
fermionic blocks; the six cross-block Frobenius products vanish identically \
by Schur orthogonality, telling the contraction engine which products to \
skip.", "TI"]
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"19d6af40-7eed-424e-b1c7-5c4f7b099a9f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The block decomposition is not just a vector-space identity: it makes inner \
products block-diagonal. The Frobenius (Hilbert-Schmidt) contraction ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"\[LeftAngleBracket]", 
     RowBox[{
      StyleBox["T", "TI"], ",", 
      StyleBox["S", "TI"]}], "\[RightAngleBracket]"}], "\[LongEqual]", 
    UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"i", "j", "k"}], "TI"],
     LimitsPositioning->True], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["T", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"i", "j", "k"}], "TI"]], 
    SubscriptBox[
     StyleBox["S", "TI"], 
     StyleBox[
      RowBox[{"i", "j", "k"}], "TI"]]}], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",
  ExpressionUUID->"03ab5287-fb76-457f-80ec-b6f3100466b8"],
 " between two rank-3 tensors on the same bond splits into a sum of three \
within-block pieces, with every cross-block term zero. This is the rank-3 \
analogue of the rank-2 block-sparse trace, and it is the workhorse identity \
behind symmetry-resolved tensor-network contractions: a network of symmetric \
tensors decomposes into a direct sum of smaller networks, one per irreducible \
representation."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7ed39f16-1d18-45b8-9569-44410c68c3e8"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[TextData[{
 "Build a second random rank-3 tensor ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   StyleBox["S", "TI"], TraditionalForm]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "26cc4604-71c4-47b2-948f-a5a81dc6426e"],
 " on the same ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    StyleBox["d", "TI"], "\[LongEqual]", "2"}], TraditionalForm]], 
  "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->"90d80532-a03f-4ef7-a7c6-8fdecd31797c"],
 " bond."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1b1cccb2-f552-4b40-8409-021b40e8abd7"],

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"SeedRandom", "[", "200", "]"}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"S3", " ", "=", " ", 
   RowBox[{"RandomReal", "[", 
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"-", "1"}], ",", " ", "1"}], "}"}], ",", " ", 
     RowBox[{"{", 
      RowBox[{"2", ",", " ", "2", ",", " ", "2"}], "}"}]}], "]"}]}], 
  ";"}]}], "Input",
 CellLabel->
  "In[387]:=",ExpressionUUID->"b279933d-74da-477b-85fd-8a09f02b2b05"]
}, Open  ]],

